---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalLayout from '@components/article/LegalLayout.astro';
import { ASSESSMENT_SUMMARY, INDEPENDENCE_MECHANISM, PAID_LINK_NOTE, methodologyHref } from '@lib/methodology';
import { buildCategorySchema, buildMeta } from '@lib/seo';

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: 'Affiliate disclaimer',
  description:
    'SleekDrops earns a commission when you buy through affiliate links. Products are researched from published evidence rather than tested hands-on, and a commission never affects a score or a pick.',
  pathname: '/disclaimer',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  {...meta}
  schema={buildCategorySchema('Affiliate disclaimer', '/disclaimer', meta.description)}
  screen="disclaimer"
>
  <LegalLayout
    eyebrow="Legal"
    titleHtml="Affiliate <em>disclaimer</em>."
    updated="October 2, 2026"
    toc={[
      { href: '#summary',    label: 'Plain summary' },
      { href: '#how',        label: 'How affiliate links work' },
      { href: '#independence', label: 'Editorial independence' },
      { href: '#testing',    label: 'What a pick rests on' },
      { href: '#labelling',  label: 'How links are labelled' },
      { href: '#corrections', label: 'Corrections' },
    ]}
  >
    <div class="summary" id="summary">
      <strong>Plain summary</strong>
      Most product links on SleekDrops are affiliate links. We earn a small commission if you buy — at no extra cost to you. Editorial choices come first; the link is what we do after we've decided what to recommend.
    </div>

    <h2 id="how">How affiliate links <em>work</em></h2>
    <p>When you click an affiliate product link on SleekDrops, you're currently sent to Amazon. If you make a qualifying purchase within its cookie window, Amazon attributes the sale to SleekDrops and pays us a small commission. The price you pay is the same — the retailer absorbs the commission out of its margin, not your wallet.</p>
    <p>Prices are not quoted from Amazon. Amazon's programme only allows prices drawn live from its own systems, so we point you to the current price instead; where a figure matters we give the manufacturer's RRP with its year.</p>

    <h2 id="independence">Editorial <em>independence</em></h2>
    <p>We don't take sponsorships. We don't run "promoted" or "sponsored" posts. No brand or PR agency pays us to publish, and no brand has approval or pre-view rights over SleekDrops coverage. The recommendation comes first; the affiliate link is added after we've decided what to recommend.</p>
    <p>That is a mechanism, not a slogan:</p>
    <ul>
      {INDEPENDENCE_MECHANISM.map((sentence) => <li>{sentence}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>When a brand supplies a product, the piece says so, and we return the unit or disclose ongoing access in the byline. The full independence policy is on <a href={methodologyHref('independence')}>how we rate</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="testing">What a pick <em>rests on</em></h2>
    <p>{ASSESSMENT_SUMMARY}</p>
    <p>How a product is assessed, what each score band means and which version of the method scored it are published in one place, on <a href={methodologyHref('assessment')}>how we rate</a>. The evidence standard behind every source is on <a href="/how-we-research">how we research</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="labelling">How links are <em>labelled</em></h2>
    <p>Every affiliate link carries <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the HTML, per Google's guidance, and every page with one opens with a disclosure under the byline. A review's buy buttons also carry the line "{PAID_LINK_NOTE}" beside them. Buttons and links that say "Check price on Amazon", "See it on Amazon" or similar are always affiliate and always go to Amazon; in-body text links to manufacturers, standards bodies and other sources are not.</p>

    <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
    <p>Spotted a mistake — a stale price, an old promo code, or a claim that no longer holds? Tell us at <a href="mailto:corrections@sleekdrops.com">corrections@sleekdrops.com</a> and we'll update the post (and credit you in the footer if you'd like).</p>
  </LegalLayout>
</BaseLayout>
